  "narrative": "I now have sufficient evidence to write the narrative. The enrichment analysis, pathway membership confirmations, and KEGG reaction-path verification are all in hand.\n\n---\n\n**Pathway-level interpretation of a steroid metabolomics signature**\n\nThe RaMP enrichment analysis of the ten differentially-abundant metabolites returns an unambiguous top result: five compounds — dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA, C01227), androstenedione (C00280), testosterone (C00535), dihydrotestosterone (DHT, C03917), and estrone (C00468) — all map to the KEGG **Androgen and Estrogen Metabolism** pathway (map00150) and the Reactome **Androgen biosynthesis** pathway, with FDR = 0.0 and fold-enrichment > 2 000. No other pathway reaches significance for the remaining five metabolites (coumarin, spironolactone, 3-hydroxy-L-proline, pyrocatechol, doxycycline), indicating that the treatment effect is specifically centred on steroid hormone biosynthesis and interconversion.\n\n**Key driver compounds.** DHEA (C01227) and androstenedione (C00280) are the most upstream intermediates in the observed steroid cluster. DHEA feeds into both the androgen and the estrogen arms of the pathway; androstenedione sits at the branch point from which testosterone and estrone are directly derived. DHT (C03917), the most downstream androgen measured here, is confirmed as reachable via the two-step path **Androstenedione → Testosterone → DHT** (KEGG BFS, 2 hops), confirming a canonical biosynthetic cascade. The co-enrichment of estrone alongside the androgens is consistent with the shared early steps of steroidogenesis and the bidirectional connectivity of these intermediates.\n\n**Biological significance.** Coordinated perturbations across this five-metabolite panel are consistent with altered activity of CYP17A1, HSD3B, or HSD17B family enzymes — the principal gatekeepers of the androgen/estrogen branch point. In prostate, breast, or adrenal contexts, such a signature can indicate either increased 